  "title": "Sample two coordinates of a curve",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Sample two coordinates of a curve",
    "name_source": "document",
    "description": "The parameter t is sampled at [0,1,2]. Formulas [2*t,t^2] give the independent point pairs (0,0),(2,1),(4,4).\n\nThe parameter t is sampled at [0,1,2]. Formulas [2*t,t^2] give the independent point pairs (0,0),(2,1),(4,4).\n\nMode: execution. Profile: studio-draft. Capability: frog.studio.formula.evaluation@1; compiled owned-value service.\nExpected:\noutput-x_values (array<f64>) = [0,2,4]\noutput-y_values (array<f64>) = [0,1,4]\noutput-error (i32) = 0\n",
    "author": "",
    "automatic_versioning": false,
    "program_version": "0.0.0.0",
    "tags": ["formula", "native", "typed", "independent-oracle", "example"],
    "documentation_uri": ""
  },
